From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.media.speech: IInspectable stubs, async ids and handlers, list constraint, session timeout and events

The FIXME stubs of the first half of the DLL, done as Windows behaves:

- every GetIids lists the interfaces its object answers (factories, async
  action and operation, compilation result, session, recognizer,
  constraint, synthesizer, stream, vectors, views, iterators);
  GetTrustLevel is BaseTrust; GetRuntimeClassName names the class, and
  the collection and async names carry the element type
  (IVectorView`1<Windows.Media.SpeechSynthesis.VoiceInformation>). An
  unknown IID is E_NOINTERFACE without a FIXME.
- IAsyncInfo::Id is counted per owning recognizer, session or synthesizer
  from 1, also for operations that then fail to start; on a closed
  operation it is E_ILLEGAL_METHOD_CALL with the id set.
- IAsync*::get_Completed returns the handler that was set, also after it
  ran, with a reference; the operation keeps the handler and holds a
  second reference while it runs. Cancel on a closed operation is S_OK.
- SpeechRecognitionListConstraint: Tag (CreateWithTag, put_Tag), Type
  (List), Probability (Default, Min, Max; others E_INVALIDARG); IsEnabled
  starts TRUE.
- Continuous session: AutoStopSilenceTimeout (20 s by default, negative
  values E_INVALIDARG; no recogniser runs, so it never fires),
  StartWithModeAsync (mode validated), CancelAsync (ends the session as
  StopAsync does).
- Recognizer: add/remove for RecognitionQualityDegrading, StateChanged and
  HypothesisGenerated register handlers and return tokens (no engine, so
  nothing raises them yet).
- DllGetClassObject returns CLASS_E_CLASSNOTAVAILABLE with a NULL result.
- typed_event_handlers_clear released nothing: it now drops the handler
  references.
- tests/speech.c: todo_wine removed where it now passes.

